{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nOn 2026-09-01 the Gerrit `LLM-Review` bot on `rebar-gerrit` fail-closed reviews because root disk reached 91-95%; review clones/materializations hit ENOSPC and surfaced as `coverage-gap (review-error)`. Manual recovery required `docker builder prune -f` without `--keep-storage`, proving the automated prune could not reclaim below its 5GB build-cache floor. Operator approved implementing both fixes A+B.\n\n## Root cause\n\n1. `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` always runs `docker builder prune -f --keep-storage \"$BUILD_CACHE_KEEP\"` (`BUILD_CACHE_KEEP=5GB`), even on acute pressure/no-op tick paths. At the incident cache size (5.244GB), automated prune freed ~0.\n2. The review hot path starts clones/materializations without checking free disk first. In particular, `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py` clones into `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"reviewbot-\")` on the root temp volume, while `repo_snapshot.py` materializes into the snapshot-store volume.\n\n## Approved implementation plan\n\n### A. Acute pressure reclaim tier\n\nKeep normal warm-cache behavior unchanged. Add `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT` default 90, above existing soft `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT=80`. When root used-% is at or above the hard threshold, `prune_docker_caches()` escalates BuildKit reclaim to `docker builder prune -f` with keep->0 (no `--keep-storage`), best-effort/non-fatal and `timeout 120` bounded like existing docker calls. Measure before/after root filesystem bytes and log bytes actually freed; success evidence is `bytes_freed > 0`, not invocation.\n\n### B. Low-disk admission control\n\nAdd a target-path free-space helper in `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py` (`shutil.disk_usage(path)`) and `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB` default 2. This independent knob is a hard pre-clone admission floor; existing janitor watermarks remain cleanup targets.\n\nCheck the target volume before cloning/materializing:\n\n- In `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py`, immediately before `TemporaryDirectory` / `gc.clone_change_ref`, measure `tempfile.gettempdir()`.\n- In `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py` / `src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py`, measure the snapshot-store path before attested snapshot clone/materialize.\n\nBelow the floor, do not clone. For the Gerrit voter, synthesize a decision with `verdict=\"BLOCK\"`, `gap_reason=\"low-disk\"`, and a first-line message using the existing tag grammar: `[LLM-Review: BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)] ...`. Define `_TAG_SUFFIXES[\"low-disk\"] = \"BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)\"` and add `low-disk` to `adapter.RETRYABLE_GAP_REASONS`; keep `retrigger.py` parsing compatible.\n\nIn `_handle_retryable_gap`, add an explicit `low-disk` arm: under budget it defers vote-less exactly like existing ADR 0069 retryable gaps; at/over the low-disk budget it returns/logs a distinct no-vote exhausted-deferral result (`gap_reason=\"low-disk\"`, labels unchanged). It must skip `append_retries_exhausted_note`, skip fail-closed `LLM-Review -1`, and skip `VOTER_ERROR` for low-disk only. Existing exhaustion behavior for non-low-disk review errors/coverage gaps is unchanged. Document this special case in ADR 0069, ADR 0077, `docs/review-policy.md`, and `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Hard-pressure reclaim: with root used-% >= `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT` and enough reclaimable build-cache excess, automated reclaim uses emergency keep->0 builder prune, measures/logs `bytes_freed > 0`, and the test fixture returns below soft `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT`; proof in `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py` and/or `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py`.\n- [ ] Warm-cache regression: below `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT`, `prune_docker_caches()` still uses `--keep-storage \"$BUILD_CACHE_KEEP\"`; proof in `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py`.\n- [ ] Review-bot low-disk admission: when `tempfile.gettempdir()` free space is below `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB`, `voter.py` does not create the clone and defers retryably/vote-less through ADR 0069; proof by focused voter test simulating low free space and asserting no clone/vote.\n- [ ] Exhausted low-disk budget: if low-disk retries are exhausted, labels remain unchanged/no `LLM-Review -1`; proof by focused voter test contrasting `gap_reason=\"low-disk\"` with ordinary `gap_reason=\"review-error\"` exhaustion.\n- [ ] Snapshot low-disk admission: when the snapshot-store volume is below `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB`, snapshot materialization aborts before clone with a retryable low-disk condition; proof around `repo_snapshot.py` / `gate_source.py`.\n- [ ] Distinct semantics: `low-disk` uses literal suffix `BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)` and is distinct from genuine coverage/review errors; proof by tag/vocabulary and routing tests.\n- [ ] Portability: all reclaim/admission logic is in-process/operation-linked, with no CI-provider dependency.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest <focused low-disk review admission/voter tests> -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n\n## File impact\n\n`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`; `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py`; `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py`; `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py`; `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`; `src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py`; `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py`; `src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py`; `src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py`; `docs/review-policy.md`; `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`; `docs/adr/0069-retryable-coverage-gap-bounded-deferral.md`; `docs/adr/0077-code-review-voter-four-pass-rewire.md`; focused tests."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788310820601733382,"uuid":"ed8db782-257a-4c6b-8126-921b2a776202"}